## std/oracle.pengu
## Contenedores de valor opcional (`maybe T`) y de cómputo falible
## (`result of T to E`): constructores, inspección, transformación,
## recuperación y conversión.
##
## Cada operación existe dos veces, con la misma semántica: como método
## (`calling m.map with f`) y como función de módulo
## (`calling oracle.map_maybe with m, f`).
##
## ## Memory
## `maybe T` y `result of T to E` poseen su carga. Ninguna función devuelve
## `self` ni un parámetro contenedor tal cual: se reconstruye el contenedor
## (`some v`, `ok v`, `err e`, `maybe none`). Los `list` devueltos los libera el
## llamante con `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## import std.oracle
## var port as maybe int is calling oracle.some_of with 8080
## var label as string is calling port.describe
## ```
##
## ## Notas de diseño
## - **No hay tuplas.** Las operaciones que devuelven dos valores usan los
##   runes genéricos `Pair` y `Triple`, definidos en este módulo
##   (`oracle.Pair of int and string`); `Pair` deriva `Par`, `Vinculum`,
##   `Imago` y `Nexus` para compararse y usarse como clave de `map`.
## - **Deprecación documental, no aplicada.** El toolchain *sí* soporta el
##   atributo real `@deprecated("Use X instead")` (emite `W0006`), pero estos
##   alias usan por ahora la convención de docstring `## @deprecated Use X
##   instead.` y por tanto **no** emiten aviso. Aplicarlo requeriría migrar
##   antes los usos internos (`result_ok_string`/`result_err_string` en
##   `std.seal` y `std.ward`, `maybe_some_string` en `std.precis`); está
##   planificado para 1.1 y el inventario con reemplazo y versión de retirada
##   vive en `docs/DEPRECATIONS.md`.
## - **Constructores de `result`.** `ok_of` / `err_of` son intrínsecos del
##   compilador (formas desnuda y `oracle.ok_of` / `oracle.err_of`) y exigen
##   contexto de tipo (`as result of T to E` o un `return` en una `weave` que
##   declara ese tipo). No se definen aquí.
## - **`where` no existe en métodos**, así que las operaciones que necesitan
##   un bound viven como `weave shard T where T: ...` de módulo.
## - **Parámetros de tipo sólo en el retorno.** `none_of shard T` no puede
##   inferir `T` (E0005): hay que pasar el argumento explícito
##   (`calling none_of of int`); por eso se conservan `none_int`,
##   `none_string`, `none_float` y `none_bool`.
## - **`flatten`** no puede colapsar `maybe maybe U` (el shard se liga al
##   elemento del receptor y no hay `where` en métodos): repaqueta la carga en
##   un contenedor nuevo. Para encadenar de verdad usa `and_then`.
## - **Funciones de módulo directas y con sufijo.** Un `weave shard T` que
##   delega en un método genérico genera C sin especializar, y un `weave`
##   `<familia>_<método>` se confunde con una especialización del método; de
##   ahí los sufijos (`unwrap_maybe`) y la lógica reimplementada.
## - **Sin move semantics.** Devolver un parámetro contenedor tal cual
##   (`return m`) provoca doble free; de ahí la reconstrucción sistemática.
## - **Tests internos.** El harness es privado (`_expect*` sobre
##   `spark.panic`) porque `import std.ward` crearía un ciclo (E0004).

# --- Imports ------------------------------------------------------------
const ORACLE_VERSION as string is "2.0.0"

import std.spark

# --- Tipos --------------------------------------------------------------

## Par genérico de valores; base de toda operación que devuelve dos cosas.
rune Pair shard A and B derive Par, Vinculum, Imago, Nexus:
    first as A
    second as B

## Terna genérica de valores; se usa para particiones de tres vías.
rune Triple shard A and B and C derive Par, Vinculum, Imago, Nexus:
    first as A
    second as B
    third as C

# --- Enchantings --------------------------------------------------------

## Métodos genéricos de `maybe T`: consulta, extracción, transformación y
## conversión. Se invocan como `calling m.map with f`.
enchanting maybe shard T:
    ## True cuando el contenedor guarda un valor (alias de `is_present`).
    weave is_some into bool:
        return (essence of self).is_present

    ## True cuando el contenedor está vacío.
    weave is_none into bool:
        return not (essence of self).is_present

    ## Devuelve el valor guardado.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Devuelve una copia de la carga; el contenedor sigue siendo válido.
    ##
    ## Panickea si el contenedor está vacío (precondición: `is_some`).
    weave unwrap into T:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            return v
        calling spark.panic with "Unwrapped none maybe"
        return (calling self.unwrap)

    ## Devuelve el valor guardado o `fallback` cuando está vacío.
    weave unwrap_or with fallback as T into T:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            return v
        return fallback

    ## Devuelve el valor guardado o el resultado de invocar `f`.
    weave unwrap_or_else with f as weave into T into T:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            return v
        return calling f

    ## Devuelve el valor guardado o panickea con `message` si está vacío.
    weave expect with message as string into T:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            return v
        calling spark.panic with message
        return (calling self.expect with message)

    ## Alias de `unwrap_or`: valor guardado o `fallback`.
    weave value_or with fallback as T into T:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            return v
        return fallback

    ## Transforma la carga con `f`, manteniendo el contenedor.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var doble as maybe int is calling m.map with double_it
    ## ```
    weave map shard U with f as weave with x as T into U into maybe U:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            return some (calling f with v)
        return maybe none

    ## Conserva la carga solo cuando `predicate` devuelve `true`.
    weave filter with predicate as weave with x as T into bool into maybe T:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            var keep as bool is calling predicate with v
            if keep:
                return some v
        return maybe none

    ## Encadena `f`, que produce a su vez un `maybe U` (evita anidar).
    weave and_then shard U with f as weave with x as T into maybe U into maybe U:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            var nxt as maybe U is calling f with v
            if w as U is nxt:
                return some w
        return maybe none

    ## Devuelve este contenedor si tiene valor; si no, `fallback`.
    weave or_else with fallback as maybe T into maybe T:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            return some v
        if w as T is fallback:
            return some w
        return maybe none

    ## Devuelve `other` solo cuando este contenedor tiene valor.
    weave and with other as maybe T into maybe T:
        if (essence of self).is_present:
            if w as T is other:
                return some w
        return maybe none

    ## Devuelve este contenedor si tiene valor; si no, `other`.
    weave or with other as maybe T into maybe T:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            return some v
        if w as T is other:
            return some w
        return maybe none

    ## Promueve a `result of T to string`, con `error_value` como error.
    weave to_result with error_value as string into result of T to string:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            return calling ok_of with v
        return calling err_of with error_value

    ## Lista de un elemento con la carga, o lista vacía si no hay valor.
    weave to_list into list of T:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            return [v]
        return list of T

    ## Descripción legible: `some(v)` o `none`.
    weave describe into string:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            return "some({v})"
        return "none"

    ## Alias de `to_list`: la carga como lista de cero o un elemento.
    weave iter into list of T:
        if v as T is essence of self:
            return [v]
        return list of T

    ## Combina dos opcionales presentes en un `Pair`.
    weave zip shard U with other as maybe U into maybe Pair of T and U:
        if a as T is essence of self:
            if b as U is other:
                var out as Pair of T and U with:
                    set .first is a
                    set .second is b
                return some out
        return maybe none

    ## Repaqueta la carga en un contenedor nuevo (identidad estructural).
    weave flatten into maybe T:
        if inner as T is essence of self:
            return some inner
        return maybe none

## Métodos genéricos de `result of T to E`: consulta, extracción,
## transformación y conversión a `maybe`.
enchanting result of shard T to shard E:
    ## True cuando el resultado representa éxito (alias de `is_ok`).
    weave is_ok into bool:
        return (essence of self).is_ok

    ## True cuando el resultado representa un error.
    weave is_err into bool:
        return not (essence of self).is_ok

    ## Devuelve la carga de éxito.
    ##
    ## Panickea con el error almacenado si el resultado es `err`.
    weave unwrap into T:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            return owns.value
        calling spark.panic with "Unwrapped err result"
        return (calling self.unwrap)

    ## Devuelve el error almacenado.
    weave unwrap_err into E:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            calling spark.panic with "unwrap_err on ok result"
        return owns.error

    ## Devuelve la carga de éxito o `fallback` si es `err`.
    weave unwrap_or with fallback as T into T:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            return owns.value
        return fallback

    ## Devuelve la carga de éxito o `f(error)` si es `err`.
    weave unwrap_or_else with f as weave with x as E into T into T:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            return owns.value
        return calling f with owns.error

    ## Devuelve la carga de éxito o panickea con `message` si es `err`.
    weave expect with message as string into T:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            return owns.value
        calling spark.panic with message
        return (calling self.expect with message)

    ## Devuelve el error o panickea con `message` si el resultado es `ok`.
    weave expect_err with message as string into E:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            calling spark.panic with message
        return owns.error

    ## Transforma la carga de éxito con `f`, propagando el error.
    weave map shard U with f as weave with x as T into U into result of U to E:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            return calling ok_of with (calling f with owns.value)
        return calling err_of with owns.error

    ## Transforma el error con `f`, propagando el éxito.
    weave map_err shard F with f as weave with x as E into F into result of T to F:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            return calling ok_of with owns.value
        return calling err_of with (calling f with owns.error)

    ## Encadena `f` sobre la carga de éxito, propagando el error.
    weave and_then shard U with f as weave with x as T into result of U to E into result of U to E:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            var nxt as result of U to E is calling f with owns.value
            if nxt.is_ok:
                return calling ok_of with nxt.value
            return calling err_of with nxt.error
        return calling err_of with owns.error

    ## Devuelve este resultado si es `ok`; si es `err`, `fallback`.
    weave or_else with fallback as result of T to E into result of T to E:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            return calling ok_of with owns.value
        if fallback.is_ok:
            return calling ok_of with fallback.value
        return calling err_of with fallback.error

    ## Descarta el error: `maybe` con la carga de éxito.
    weave ok into maybe T:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            return some owns.value
        return maybe none

    ## Descarta el éxito: `maybe` con el error.
    weave err into maybe E:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            return maybe none
        return some owns.error

    ## Alias de `ok`: la carga de éxito como `maybe T`.
    weave to_maybe into maybe T:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            return some owns.value
        return maybe none

    ## Lista de un elemento con la carga de éxito, o vacía si es `err`.
    weave to_list into list of T:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            return [owns.value]
        return list of T

    ## Descripción legible: `ok(v)` o `err(e)`.
    weave describe into string:
        var owns as result of T to E is essence of self
        if owns.is_ok:
            return "ok({owns.value})"
        return "err({owns.error})"

# --- Tipos legados (compatibilidad 0.14.x) ------------------------------

## @deprecated Optional entero legado (campo `is_present` + `value`). Usa `maybe T` / `result of T to E`.
## Optional entero legado (campo `is_present` + `value`).
rune MaybeInt:
    is_present as bool
    value as int

# Optional float: `is_present` is true when a value is stored, `value` holds
# it (0.0 when none).
## @deprecated Optional flotante legado (campo `is_present` + `value`). Usa `maybe T` / `result of T to E`.
## Optional flotante legado (campo `is_present` + `value`).
rune MaybeFloat:
    is_present as bool
    value as float

# Optional string: `is_present` is true when a value is stored, `value` holds
# it ("" when none). The payload string is owned by the wrapper.
## @deprecated Optional string legado (campo `is_present` + `value`). Usa `maybe T` / `result of T to E`.
## Optional string legado (campo `is_present` + `value`).
rune MaybeString:
    is_present as bool
    value as string

# Fallible int: `is_ok` is true when `value` is meaningful; false means the
# operation failed and `error_msg` describes why.
## @deprecated Resultado entero legado (`is_ok`, `value`, `error_msg`). Usa `maybe T` / `result of T to E`.
## Resultado entero legado (`is_ok`, `value`, `error_msg`).
rune ResultInt:
    is_ok as bool
    value as int
    error_msg as string

# Fallible string: `is_ok` is true when `value` is meaningful; false means the
# operation failed and `error_msg` describes why. The payload string is owned
# by the wrapper.
## @deprecated Resultado string legado (`is_ok`, `value`, `error_msg`). Usa `maybe T` / `result of T to E`.
## Resultado string legado (`is_ok`, `value`, `error_msg`).
rune ResultString:
    is_ok as bool
    value as string
    error_msg as string

# --- Enchantings legados (compatibilidad 0.14.x) ------------------------

## @deprecated Use `enchanting maybe shard T` instead.
## Métodos legados de `MaybeInt` (compatibilidad 0.14.x).
enchanting MaybeInt:
    # True when the wrapper holds a value (mirrors the is_present field).
    weave is_present into bool:
        return self->is_present

    # True when the wrapper is empty (no value stored).
    weave is_none into bool:
        return judge self->is_present:
            when true -> false
            when false -> true

    # Returns the stored value, or panics with "Unwrapped none MaybeInt" when
    # the wrapper is empty.
    weave unwrap into int:
        if self->is_present:
            return self->value
        calling spark.panic with "Unwrapped none MaybeInt"
        return 0

    # Returns the stored value when present, otherwise `default_val`.
    weave unwrap_or with default_val as int into int:
        return judge self->is_present:
            when true -> self->value
            when false -> default_val

# Methods on MaybeString values, invoked as `calling m.is_present` / `m.unwrap`.
## @deprecated Use `enchanting maybe shard T` instead.
## Métodos legados de `MaybeString` (compatibilidad 0.14.x).
enchanting MaybeString:
    # True when the wrapper holds a value (mirrors the is_present field).
    weave is_present into bool:
        return self->is_present

    # True when the wrapper is empty (no value stored).
    weave is_none into bool:
        return judge self->is_present:
            when true -> false
            when false -> true

    # Returns the stored value, or panics with "Unwrapped none MaybeString"
    # when the wrapper is empty.
    weave unwrap into string:
        if self->is_present:
            return self->value
        calling spark.panic with "Unwrapped none MaybeString"
        return ""

    # Returns the stored value when present, otherwise `default_val`.
    weave unwrap_or with default_val as string into string:
        return judge self->is_present:
            when true -> self->value
            when false -> default_val

# Methods on ResultInt values, invoked as `calling r.is_ok` / `r.unwrap`.
## @deprecated Use `enchanting result of shard T to shard E` instead.
## Métodos legados de `ResultInt` (compatibilidad 0.14.x).
enchanting ResultInt:
    # True when the result holds a value (mirrors the is_ok field).
    weave is_ok into bool:
        return self->is_ok

    # True when the result carries an error (no value stored).
    weave is_err into bool:
        return judge self->is_ok:
            when true -> false
            when false -> true

    # Returns the ok value, or panics with the stored error message when the
    # result is err.
    weave unwrap into int:
        if self->is_ok:
            return self->value
        calling spark.panic with self->error_msg
        return 0

    # Returns the error message ("" when the result is ok).
    weave unwrap_err into string:
        return self->error_msg

    # Returns the ok value when present, otherwise `default_val`.
    weave unwrap_or with default_val as int into int:
        return judge self->is_ok:
            when true -> self->value
            when false -> default_val

# Methods on ResultString values, invoked as `calling r.is_ok` / `r.unwrap`.
## @deprecated Use `enchanting result of shard T to shard E` instead.
## Métodos legados de `ResultString` (compatibilidad 0.14.x).
enchanting ResultString:
    # True when the result holds a value (mirrors the is_ok field).
    weave is_ok into bool:
        return self->is_ok

    # True when the result carries an error (no value stored).
    weave is_err into bool:
        return judge self->is_ok:
            when true -> false
            when false -> true

    # Returns the ok value, or panics with the stored error message when the
    # result is err.
    weave unwrap into string:
        if self->is_ok:
            return self->value
        calling spark.panic with self->error_msg
        return ""

    # Returns the error message ("" when the result is ok).
    weave unwrap_err into string:
        return self->error_msg

    # Returns the ok value when present, otherwise `default_val`.
    weave unwrap_or with default_val as string into string:
        return judge self->is_ok:
            when true -> self->value
            when false -> default_val

# --- Funciones legadas de módulo (compatibilidad 0.14.x) ----------------

## @deprecated Use `oracle.some_of shard T` instead.
weave maybe_some_int with val as int into MaybeInt:
    return with is_present is true , value is val

## @deprecated Use `oracle.none_of of int` instead.
weave maybe_none_int into MaybeInt:
    return with is_present is false , value is 0

## @deprecated Use `oracle.some_of shard T` instead.
weave maybe_some_string with val as string into MaybeString:
    return with is_present is true , value is val

## @deprecated Use `oracle.none_of of string` instead.
weave maybe_none_string into MaybeString:
    return with is_present is false , value is ""

## @deprecated Use the `ok_of` intrinsic (`calling ok_of with v`) instead.
weave result_ok_int with val as int into ResultInt:
    return with is_ok is true , value is val , error_msg is ""

## @deprecated Use the `err_of` intrinsic (`calling err_of with e`) instead.
weave result_err_int with msg as string into ResultInt:
    return with is_ok is false , value is 0 , error_msg is msg

## @deprecated Use the `ok_of` intrinsic (`calling ok_of with v`) instead.
weave result_ok_string with val as string into ResultString:
    return with is_ok is true , value is val , error_msg is ""

## @deprecated Use the `err_of` intrinsic (`calling err_of with e`) instead.
weave result_err_string with msg as string into ResultString:
    return with is_ok is false , value is "" , error_msg is msg

